      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آدَبُ</span></b>  [originally <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَأْدَبُ</span>, <i>More,</i> or <i>most, characterized by what is termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدَب</span>; i. e. <i>better,</i> or
<i>best, disciplined, educated, bred,</i> or <i>mannered;
more,</i> or <i>most, polite;</i> &amp;c.]. You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَمِنْ آدَبِ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّاسِ</span> [<i>He is of the best disciplined,</i> &amp;c., <i>of
men</i>]. (A.)

